TI  - Development of a Natural Language Processing System to Identify Clinical 
      Documentation of Electronic Cigarette Use.
PG  - 659-663
LID - 10.3233/SHTI231047 [doi]
AB  - Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems (ENDS) use has increased substantially in 
      the United States since 2010. To date, there is limited evidence regarding the 
      nature and extent of ENDS documentation in the clinical note. In this work we 
      investigate the effectiveness of different approaches to identify a patient's 
      documented ENDS use. We report on the development and validation of a natural 
      language processing system to identify patients with explicit documentation of 
      ENDS using a large national cohort of patients at the United States Department of 
      Veterans Affairs.
