IS  - 1879-8365 (Electronic)
IS  - 0926-9630 (Linking)
VI  - 336
DP  - 2026 May 21
TI  - Voice Diaries as Digital Biomarkers: A Scoping Review.
PG  - 1090-1091
LID - 10.3233/SHTI260365 [doi]
AB  - Our goal in this review is to map how voice diaries are used as digital 
      biomarkers, summarize computational pipelines, and identify methodological gaps. 
      Seven databases were searched using the Population-Concept-Context framework. 
      10/41 records met inclusion criteria. Most studies used transcripts (7/10); few 
      analyzed audio (3/10), one used a multimodal approach with text, audio, and 
      sensor data. Methods spanned lexicon-based, machine learning, and LLM approaches. 
      Validation was inconsistent. Computational analysis of voice diaries is promising 
      but early-stage and text-based requiring transparent methods and rigorous 
      validation.
