TI  - Accent related errors in clinical speech transcription and a LLM-based remedy.
LID - 10.1038/s41746-026-02490-z [doi]
LID - 297
AB  - Accurate clinical documentation is essential for safe, effective patient care. AI 
      tools powered by automatic speech recognition can streamline this process. 
      Variable performance across speakers with diverse accents leads to transcription 
      errors and clinical risk. In testing Whisper and WhisperX on native and 
      non-native English clinical speech, error rates were significantly higher for 
      non-native speakers. Post-processing with GPT-4o restored lost accuracy. This 
      chained approach (WhisperX-GPT) reduced accent-related errors.
