DP  - 2026 Jun 3
TI  - AI-Driven Heart Failure Decision Support in Skilled Nursing Facilities.
PG  - 108561
LID - S2666-0849(26)01720-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jaccas.2026.108561 [doi]
AB  - Heart failure management in skilled nursing facilities (SNFs) is complicated by 
      limited access to specialists, incomplete clinical documentation, and patients 
      with complex comorbidities. Artificial intelligence clinical decision support 
      systems have been developed mostly for acute hospital settings but not for SNF 
      settings. We present ForeSight-HF, an artificial intelligence clinical decision 
      support tool designed specifically for SNF heart failure management. Built on a 
      large language model with HIPAA-compliant infrastructure, ForeSight-HF 
      synthesizes unstructured clinical documentation to generate heart failure 
      likelihood scores, exacerbation risk scores, and individualized management 
      recommendations. We illustrate its utility through 2 contrasting cases: a 
      Warm/Wet (congested, well-perfused) patient for whom the system recommended 
      intensified diuresis, and a Cold/Dry (hypovolemic, hypoperfused) patient for whom 
      it recommended diuretic de-escalation to prevent harm. ForeSight-HF may help 
      close a persistent care gap in postacute heart failure management.
